<Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

<p>From Cherry Creek and Wash Park to the Highlands and the southern suburbs, Denver kitchens lean transitional — painted-and-stained two-tone schemes, walnut or white-oak islands, and a growing appetite for handleless European fronts in higher-end remodels.</p>
<h2 id="denver-kitchen-showrooms">Denver Kitchen Showrooms</h2>
<p>Pinnacle Sales brands are sold through independent local showrooms in and around Denver. Tell us about your project and we'll connect you with the nearest authorized dealer.</p>
<p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/contact">Find a Local Dealer</a></p>
<h2 id="best-cabinet-lines-for-denver-kitchens">Best Cabinet Lines for Denver Kitchens</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong><a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry">Shiloh Cabinetry</a></strong> — The most versatile choice for Denver's transitional look: custom paint, broad wood species, face-frame and <a href="/playbook/modern-inset">inset</a> options.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry">Eclipse Cabinetry</a></strong> — Frameless, full-access for clean contemporary Denver remodels that need maximum storage.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/brands/pronorm-german-kitchens">Pronorm German Kitchens</a></strong> — Handleless, precision-engineered fronts for high-end Cherry Creek and Cherry Hills projects.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/brands/aspect-cabinetry">Aspect Cabinetry</a></strong> — Semi-custom value for builder and investment-property kitchens.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="denver-kitchen-design-trends">Denver Kitchen Design Trends</h2>
<p>The Denver metro favors transitional kitchens that pair painted uppers (white, greige, soft black) with warm walnut or natural-oak islands and lowers. Two-tone schemes dominate, and inset construction is increasingly requested for its furniture-quality look. In luxury pockets — Cherry Creek, Cherry Hills Village, Hilltop — handleless German systems and slab-front contemporary kitchens are gaining ground.</p>
